{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai narrative ai narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md","fileName":"AI Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Narrative","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Superintelligence","AI Control Problem","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ai narrative ai narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md","fileName":"AI Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"AI Narrative","heading":"AI Narrative","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An AI narrative is a recurring story that frames what artificial intelligence is likely to become and how people should respond to it. Stories of obedient servants, rebellious creations, machine domination, or technological salvation shape public expectations before a specific system is evaluated.\n\nNarratives can direct attention and policy. A future-oriented story about [[Superintelligence]] may highlight the [[AI Control Problem]], while also distracting from harms caused by present systems. Narratives differ across cultures, so treating one familiar Western story as a universal forecast can hide alternative relationships between humans and technology.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","Superintelligence","AI Control Problem","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/AI Narrative.md"